  "knowledge": {
    "progressSummary": "COMPLETE: proved the three standard formulations of Firoozbakht are equivalent (verified, 0 axioms). The conjecture itself is untouched and remains open.",
    "builtItems": [
      "root_lt_iff (BoundedPrimeGapsOQ05.lean): root inequality a^{1/(n+1)} < b^{1/n} ⟺ core a^n < b^{n+1} for positive reals, n≥1",
      "rpow_lt_iff (BoundedPrimeGapsOQ05.lean): a < b^{1+1/n} ⟺ same core a^n < b^{n+1}",
      "core_real_iff_nat (BoundedPrimeGapsOQ05.lean): real-rpow core ⟺ natural-number inequality p^n < q^{n+1}",
      "FiroozbakhtRoot / FiroozbakhtRpow / FiroozbakhtIntPow (BoundedPrimeGapsOQ05.lean): the three prime formulations",
      "firoozbakht_forms_tfae (BoundedPrimeGapsOQ05.lean): List.TFAE of the three formulations"
    ],
    "insights": [
      "All three inequalities are strictly-monotone images of the single core a^n < b^{n+1}: ROOT via power 1/(n(n+1)), RPOW via power 1/n; strict monotonicity of x↦x^c (c>0) makes each a genuine iff.",
      "The integer-power form is the most elementary — for primes it is a statement purely in ℕ (p_{n+1}^n < p_n^{n+1}), needing no real analysis to state.",
      "Axiom-freeness comes precisely from asserting only the equivalence, not the conjecture: the file uses Real.rpow_lt_rpow_iff + Real.rpow_mul + rpow_natCast, all foundational."
    ],
